hi we are phillip and jens from otto  since november 2020 we have been working  as part of team archie to explore new  opportunities of information retrieval  systems  the auto group is germany's second  biggest e-commerce player and with 15.6  billion euro turnover one of the biggest  e-commerce player in the world  otto has one of the biggest e-commerce  data science communities in europe with  machine learning being part of almost  all e-commerce capabilities  part of our approach has been developing  a transformer-based semantic search  one of our bigger challenges was the  performance and scalability of our  transformer modules with a target to use  it on our platform a real-time scenario  for transformer models on the highest  load  in total it took us less than one day to  set everything up from our side in the  first step we pushed our models through  the hugging phase model hub  the model's inference we are then  optimized for our hardware by hugging  phase and the result provided in a  docker container that just needed to be  started  the api was callable within a couple of  minutes and we could start our  evaluation process  we trained the roberta model with the  whole product variations of our platform  and the ranking model as downstream  tasks  we were able to reach around 2.3  milliseconds for the feature extraction  task and around 2.4 milliseconds for the  ranking task per data point  this is about 100 times faster than a  non-optimized model on cpu and 10 times  faster than on gpu  batch processing and multi gpu were not  available at the time  we expect these features to contribute  to even better performance especially  for the ranking task  we found the major benefit for us and a  tremendous increase in research and  model evaluation cycles  besides the fact that with infinity for  the first time transformer models can  easily be used in real-time scenarios
 

